        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Edits a group of caller/callee graphs with state info from &apos;ini&apos; :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   The base implementation forwards straight to #edit and **ignores &apos;ini&apos; entirely**,
   exactly as the pure-Python original does -- see
   :cpp:func:`BaseIniGraphEdit::editFromIni`&apos;s own note
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>graphGroups</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The group of graphs to edit for each .ini file, modified in place </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ini</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The associated original .ini file </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of mod to fix </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the mod to fix to. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>""</computeroutput></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The same groups that were passed in, after editing </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
